Kadir</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health and social impacts of improved stoves on rural women: a pilot intervention in Sindh, Pakistan</article-title><source>Indoor Air</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>316</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16108903</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-0668.2005.00367.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Disease Control Priorities Project</collab></person-group><article-title>Indoor Air Pollution. Key Features and Lessons from India's National Stove Program;Disease Control Priorities Project</article-title><source>Disease Control Priorities Project World Bank Group</source><year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Ethiopian Rural Household Survey</collab></person-group><article-title>Questionnaire</article-title><source>Ethiopian Rural Household Survey</source><year>1995</year></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eloundou-Enyegue</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Meekers</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Calves</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>From awareness to adoption: the effect of AIDS education and condom social marketing on condom use in Tanzania (1993&#x02013;1996)</article-title><source>J Biosoc Sci</source><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>268</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15906883</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0021932004007011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>FU</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Beneficial effects. Three ANC visits might be the divergent point in lowering low birth weight babies. Bangladesh</article-title><source>Integration</source><year>1992</year><fpage>50</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12343897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><source>Indoor Air Pollution and Health</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>World Health Organisation</publisher-name><comment>9-7-2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parvez</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Argos</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hussain</surname><given-names>AZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Momotaj</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Dhar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Prevalence of arsenic exposure from drinking water and awareness of its health risks in a Bangladeshi population: results from a large population-based study</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><year>2006</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>359</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16507457</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kotler</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaltman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Social marketing: an approach to planned social change</article-title><source>J Mark</source><year>1971</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12276120</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/1249783</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>